WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:25.002
<b><i><font color="#d9f7">Improved By: Fidel33
Sub Upload Date: October 22, 2015</font></i></b>

2
00:01:40.834 --> 00:01:42.677
Mother!

3
00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:41.690
Mom.

4
00:03:42.456 --> 00:03:43.628
Hey.

5
00:03:44.291 --> 00:03:46.293
There's something
outside my window.

6
00:03:47.561 --> 00:03:49.871
Oh, baby, you're having
a nightmare, huh?

7
00:03:51.131 --> 00:03:52.201
Okay.

8
00:03:52.432 --> 00:03:53.911
Let me put you back to bed.

9
00:03:54.735 --> 00:03:56.305
I want Daddy to do it.

10
00:03:57.471 --> 00:03:59.144
How 'bout we wait
for him together, huh?

11
00:04:00.073 --> 00:04:01.450
Come on in. Bring Bear.

12
00:04:07.247 --> 00:04:08.282
I gotcha.

13
00:04:08.548 --> 00:04:09.891
We'll keep each other safe.

14
00:04:31.905 --> 00:04:32.906
Shit.

15
00:05:30.230 --> 00:05:31.231
Hi.

16
00:05:32.465 --> 00:05:33.705
Did you figure it out?

17
00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:34.972
What?

18
00:05:35.235 --> 00:05:37.010
What you're gonna
be for Halloween.

19
00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:38.505
Maybe.

20
00:05:39.005 --> 00:05:39.965
But you're gonna have to

21
00:05:40.006 --> 00:05:41.747
wait until tomorrow to find out.

22
00:05:42.809 --> 00:05:44.083
I'll be a pirate.

23
00:05:45.645 --> 00:05:47.352
Ah, good choice.

24
00:05:47.647 --> 00:05:48.819
Mom helped me pick it out

25
00:05:48.882 --> 00:05:50.691
after we got the pumpkin.

26
00:05:51.751 --> 00:05:53.526
Mom said she'd carve it with me,

27
00:05:54.154 --> 00:05:55.758
but I wanted to wait for you.

28
00:05:55.856 --> 00:05:56.857
Oh,

29
00:05:57.090 --> 00:05:58.091
Well...

30
00:05:58.325 --> 00:05:59.497
We'll do it tomorrow,

31
00:05:59.759 --> 00:06:01.932
just before we go trick
or treating, okay?

32
00:06:02.262 --> 00:06:03.263
Promise?

33
00:06:03.663 --> 00:06:04.698
I promise.

34
00:06:05.432 --> 00:06:07.503
Now, go back to sleep.

35
00:06:12.172 --> 00:06:13.207
Oh, and Dad...

36
00:06:13.707 --> 00:06:14.742
Yes?

37
00:06:14.941 --> 00:06:16.614
Can you check
outside my window?

38
00:06:16.877 --> 00:06:18.015
I saw something.

39
00:06:20.180 --> 00:06:21.215
Sure.

40
00:06:29.422 --> 00:06:31.561
Nope, all clear.

41
00:06:32.626 --> 00:06:33.866
I love you, Dad.

42
00:06:35.762 --> 00:06:37.139
I love you too, son.

43
00:06:42.736 --> 00:06:43.806
I'm sorry.

44
00:06:44.604 --> 00:06:46.606
I'm getting tired of
going to bed without you.

45
00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:48.783
If they're on the fence,
I'm going to have to

46
00:06:48.875 --> 00:06:51.412
publish another article
as soon as I can.

47
00:06:52.479 --> 00:06:54.322
- Are they on the fence?
- I don't know.

48
00:06:55.215 --> 00:06:58.094
Just seems like I would've
received a letter by now.

49
00:07:01.121 --> 00:07:03.158
Charlie wanted to wait
up for you tonight.

50
00:07:05.659 --> 00:07:07.104
I think,

51
00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:09.640
if you don't carve that
pumpkin with him tomorrow,

52
00:07:10.764 --> 00:07:12.505
he's going to disown you.

53
00:07:13.934 --> 00:07:15.072
Can he do that?

54
00:07:16.503 --> 00:07:18.346
I think he'd have a case, yeah.

55
00:07:18.838 --> 00:07:19.839
And what about you?

56
00:07:20.273 --> 00:07:23.277
Are you ready to disown me, too?
Huh?

57
00:07:30.350 --> 00:07:31.988
Can I take that as a no?

58
00:07:32.852 --> 00:07:35.196
I don't want you to think
I'm not mad at you, okay?

59
00:07:44.998 --> 00:07:48.104
"My darling,
my darling, I see it aright.

60
00:07:48.335 --> 00:07:51.680
"Tis the aged gray willows
deceiving thy sight.

61
00:07:51.938 --> 00:07:53.383
"I love thee!"

62
00:07:54.107 --> 00:07:57.213
I'm charmed by thy
beauty, dear boy!

63
00:07:57.844 --> 00:08:01.053
And if thou'rt unwilling,
then force I'II employ.“

64
00:08:01.514 --> 00:08:03.858
“My father, my father,
he seizes me fast,

65
00:08:03.950 --> 00:08:06.658
"For sorely the Erl-King
has hurt me at last."

66
00:08:07.020 --> 00:08:10.365
The father now gallops,
with terror half wild,

67
00:08:10.657 --> 00:08:13.638
He grasps in his arms
the poor shuddering child,

68
00:08:13.693 --> 00:08:17.004
He reaches his courtyard
with toil and with dread,

69
00:08:17.063 --> 00:08:22.035
"The child in his arms
finds he motionless, dead."

70
00:08:24.371 --> 00:08:26.044
Pretty good, huh?

71
00:08:26.139 --> 00:08:27.174
Kyle.

72
00:08:27.240 --> 00:08:29.311
Who is this, uh, Earl Linking'?

73
00:08:29.376 --> 00:08:30.821
And his creepy daughters.

74
00:08:31.077 --> 00:08:32.385
We don't know for sure.

75
00:08:32.912 --> 00:08:35.324
They might be creatures
out of northern mythology.

76
00:08:35.515 --> 00:08:36.994
Or some Celtic lore.

77
00:08:37.317 --> 00:08:38.762
Or they simply stepped out

78
00:08:38.852 --> 00:08:41.662
of Johann Wolfgang von
Goethe's nightmares.

79
00:08:43.156 --> 00:08:44.430
But when you go out tonight,

80
00:08:45.058 --> 00:08:46.594
spare a thought for Lovecraft.

81
00:08:46.893 --> 00:08:48.600
For Stoker, for Poe...

82
00:08:49.229 --> 00:08:50.731
And for Goethe's Erl-King.

83
00:08:51.097 --> 00:08:52.269
'Cause they were
all bound by one

84
00:08:52.365 --> 00:08:54.845
great, and noble objective.

85
00:08:55.702 --> 00:08:57.682
To scare the living
shit out of you.

86
00:08:59.873 --> 00:09:00.851
Happy Halloween.

87
00:09:21.694 --> 00:09:22.854
Hello, hello, hello!

88
00:09:23.797 --> 00:09:24.969
Hey, Mom.

89
00:09:25.365 --> 00:09:26.708
Where's my little pirate?

90
00:09:28.134 --> 00:09:29.272
Mom, check it out.

91
00:09:33.973 --> 00:09:36.954
Wow, that's a great
indoor activity.

92
00:09:37.043 --> 00:09:38.283
- Yeah.
- You...

93
00:09:38.945 --> 00:09:39.980
You look amazing.

94
00:09:41.381 --> 00:09:42.291
He's on fire, huh?

95
00:09:42.382 --> 00:09:44.293
He's so excited.

96
00:09:44.384 --> 00:09:46.125
The pirate looks perfect,

97
00:09:46.219 --> 00:09:47.493
thank you very much.

98
00:09:47.587 --> 00:09:48.867
And we'll see you
tomorrow, yeah?

99
00:09:48.922 --> 00:09:49.832
Oh, yes.

100
00:09:49.923 --> 00:09:50.833
Happy Halloween!

101
00:09:50.924 --> 00:09:52.604
Happy Halloween
to you, too, Rosa.

102
00:09:53.093 --> 00:09:54.800
When's Dad coming home?

103
00:09:54.994 --> 00:09:57.338
He should be on his way right now.

104
00:09:57.630 --> 00:09:59.405
- Rosa take you to art class?
- Yeah.

105
00:09:59.599 --> 00:10:00.771
I wanna see.

106
00:10:02.102 --> 00:10:04.582
Charlie, that's really scary.

107
00:10:08.975 --> 00:10:10.352
You wanna tell me about that?

108
00:10:11.177 --> 00:10:13.316
That's the thing
I saw outside my window.

109
00:10:14.114 --> 00:10:15.754
I thought you told
me you couldn't see it?

110
00:10:16.116 --> 00:10:17.186
I kinda saw it.

111
00:10:17.684 --> 00:10:19.186
It just kinda looked like that.

112
00:10:21.354 --> 00:10:22.458
Can we go, already?

113
00:10:22.522 --> 00:10:23.694
Where's Dad?

114
00:10:45.111 --> 00:10:46.613
- Yeah?
- Hannah...

115
00:10:47.547 --> 00:10:50.289
Oh, Michael,
come here, come here.

116
00:10:50.984 --> 00:10:52.224
Come, look at this.

117
00:10:52.552 --> 00:10:54.998
It washed ashore last
week on Jones Beach.

118
00:10:58.658 --> 00:11:00.194
What are those, Latin numerals?

119
00:11:00.293 --> 00:11:02.830
Exactly. It's an M and a D,

120
00:11:02.896 --> 00:11:04.534
and possibly a C.

121
00:11:04.631 --> 00:11:05.701
Sixteen hundred.

122
00:11:05.798 --> 00:11:08.369
They used to engrave ships
with the year they were built,

123
00:11:08.468 --> 00:11:10.188
which means this piece
of driftwood was once

124
00:11:10.236 --> 00:11:11.874
part of the body of
a ship that helped

125
00:11:11.971 --> 00:11:14.383
settle this city 400 years ago.

126
00:11:14.474 --> 00:11:16.010
That's quite
something, isn't it?

127
00:11:17.043 --> 00:11:18.078
And so's this.

128
00:11:24.083 --> 00:11:26.154
"Dear Professor Lawford."

129
00:11:26.219 --> 00:11:27.926
Congratulations, Mike!

130
00:11:28.421 --> 00:11:29.866
You've come a long way from that

131
00:11:29.923 --> 00:11:32.904
arrogant Yank who drank
himself out of Heidelberg.

132
00:11:32.992 --> 00:11:34.562
Thanks for
recommending me, Hannah.

133
00:11:35.094 --> 00:11:37.836
You deserve it,
more than anybody.

134
00:11:41.601 --> 00:11:43.012
I've gotta go,

135
00:11:43.069 --> 00:11:44.412
I have a very important
appointment with a pirate.

136
00:11:57.217 --> 00:11:58.252
Hey.

137
00:12:10.263 --> 00:12:12.573
God, it was the most incredible
exhibit I've ever seen.

138
00:12:13.099 --> 00:12:14.635
And they, whoa,
whoa, whoa, whoa!

139
00:12:15.034 --> 00:12:17.036
Easy on the candy,
all of you, please.

140
00:12:17.103 --> 00:12:18.980
Maybe Dad
called and you missed it.

141
00:12:19.439 --> 00:12:20.474
I will try him again.

142
00:12:43.329 --> 00:12:44.740
Hi, it's Mike, leave a message,

143
00:12:44.797 --> 00:12:46.970
Hi get back to you
as soon as I can.

144
00:12:49.435 --> 00:12:50.470
Hey.

145
00:12:51.137 --> 00:12:52.172
You Okay?

146
00:12:52.839 --> 00:12:55.183
- Did you see it, Mom'?
- Did I see what?

147
00:12:56.142 --> 00:12:57.143
The bird.

148
00:12:58.011 --> 00:12:59.115
The bird?

149
00:13:00.480 --> 00:13:01.481
No.

150
00:13:02.115 --> 00:13:03.150
No, I don't.

151
00:13:17.030 --> 00:13:18.976
I think I'll be Robin Hood next year.

152
00:13:19.032 --> 00:13:21.308
He steals from the rich
and gives to the poor.

153
00:13:21.467 --> 00:13:24.107
Well, that is very noble, my little man.

154
00:13:24.537 --> 00:13:26.448
And I bet he keeps
a little extra on the side

155
00:13:26.506 --> 00:13:28.508
just to himself.

156
00:13:28.608 --> 00:13:29.552
I see.

157
00:13:35.181 --> 00:13:37.161
Mom, can we go to
the carnival, please?

158
00:13:37.717 --> 00:13:39.890
No, not this year, my man.

159
00:13:40.320 --> 00:13:43.392
I'm sorry, it is late, and
you have school tomorrow.

160
00:13:43.489 --> 00:13:45.833
Come with me.
Come on, come on my prince.

161
00:13:47.393 --> 00:13:49.031
I said, Draw, partner!

162
00:13:50.396 --> 00:13:51.374
Dad!

163
00:13:51.464 --> 00:13:52.841
You're a cowboy!

164
00:13:52.899 --> 00:13:54.173
I couldn't find
my cowboy hat,

165
00:13:54.233 --> 00:13:55.303
but boy, you guys look great.

166
00:13:55.368 --> 00:13:56.847
You make a great pirate,
Charlie.

167
00:13:56.903 --> 00:13:57.904
Where were you?

168
00:13:58.004 --> 00:13:59.210
Mom said you were
gonna meet up with us.

169
00:13:59.305 --> 00:14:00.841
I apologize, my phone died.

170
00:14:01.574 --> 00:14:02.917
Come on, let's go to bed.

171
00:14:03.643 --> 00:14:04.553
Mom,

172
00:14:04.644 --> 00:14:05.918
can we go to the carnival,

173
00:14:06.012 --> 00:14:07.855
just for a bit, please?

174
00:14:08.748 --> 00:14:09.886
Oh, let me take him.

175
00:14:10.383 --> 00:14:11.885
Just give us a half an hour.

176
00:14:12.752 --> 00:14:14.857
- Come on, Kristen.
- Okay, okay.

177
00:14:14.921 --> 00:14:16.093
Okay, but would you do me a favor

178
00:14:16.189 --> 00:14:17.167
and put him to bed, tonight?

179
00:14:17.223 --> 00:14:18.463
He is hopped up on enough sugar

180
00:14:18.491 --> 00:14:20.732
to last him until Christmas

181
00:14:20.827 --> 00:14:22.898
and I have to finish some
client designs tonight.

182
00:14:22.995 --> 00:14:24.338
- Of course.
- All right.

183
00:14:24.897 --> 00:14:25.898
I got it.

184
00:14:26.199 --> 00:14:27.200
You got what?

185
00:14:27.667 --> 00:14:28.941
Drum roll, please.

186
00:14:31.003 --> 00:14:32.107
I got tenure.

187
00:14:33.673 --> 00:14:35.880
Oh, my God!

188
00:14:35.942 --> 00:14:38.047
Oh, my God,
I'm so proud of you!

189
00:14:39.779 --> 00:14:41.417
Does this mean that we can go'?

190
00:14:42.281 --> 00:14:43.885
Yes, it means you can go.

191
00:14:44.717 --> 00:14:46.424
It means that we will
celebrate tonight.

192
00:14:46.919 --> 00:14:48.364
Everything's going
to be better now.

193
00:14:48.421 --> 00:14:50.094
You boys have fun tonight.

194
00:14:50.757 --> 00:14:51.758
Come here.

195
00:14:52.091 --> 00:14:53.593
Candy please, young man.

196
00:14:54.861 --> 00:14:56.602
- Come on, already.
- Hey, let's do it.

197
00:14:57.096 --> 00:14:58.769
- Hey, Professor?
- Uh huh?

198
00:14:59.031 --> 00:15:00.031
Keep your chaps on, yeah?

199
00:15:00.032 --> 00:15:00.942
Yeah!

200
00:15:01.033 --> 00:15:02.034
Let's go, Dad.

201
00:15:38.337 --> 00:15:39.338
Smile, Dad.

202
00:15:42.308 --> 00:15:43.343
You having fun?

203
00:15:43.976 --> 00:15:45.182
This is awesome.

204
00:15:55.121 --> 00:15:56.657
You see those skeletons?

205
00:15:57.156 --> 00:15:58.294
Pretty scary, huh'?

206
00:16:07.333 --> 00:16:08.334
Charlie?

207
00:16:12.538 --> 00:16:13.608
Okay.

208
00:16:15.274 --> 00:16:16.480
All right?

209
00:16:18.211 --> 00:16:20.282
I'm sorry we didn't
carve pumpkins together.

210
00:16:20.713 --> 00:16:21.783
It's okay.

211
00:16:22.048 --> 00:16:23.459
I know you got a
lot of work to do.

212
00:16:23.516 --> 00:16:24.494
No, it's not okay.

213
00:16:24.550 --> 00:16:25.995
I promised I'd be there,

214
00:16:26.052 --> 00:16:28.726
and promises dads make to
their sons are special things.

215
00:16:29.222 --> 00:16:30.223
You know you're
the most important

216
00:16:30.323 --> 00:16:31.666
person in the
world to me, right?

217
00:16:32.124 --> 00:16:33.194
Yeah.

218
00:16:34.460 --> 00:16:35.632
Let's get some ice cream!

219
00:16:39.465 --> 00:16:40.466
Hey.

220
00:16:41.501 --> 00:16:42.502
Charlie.

221
00:16:42.902 --> 00:16:44.074
Charlie.

222
00:16:44.170 --> 00:16:45.513
I really need you
to stay close to me,

223
00:16:45.571 --> 00:16:47.050
and I need you to look
where you're going, okay?

224
00:16:47.139 --> 00:16:48.516
Let me, let me take that.

225
00:16:50.142 --> 00:16:51.177
Come on.

226
00:16:52.712 --> 00:16:54.191
What kind of ice
cream do you want?

227
00:16:54.247 --> 00:16:56.352
Swirled cone with
rainbow sprinkles.

228
00:16:56.415 --> 00:16:57.416
Sounds good.

229
00:17:14.934 --> 00:17:15.935
Dad,

230
00:17:17.703 --> 00:17:19.512
can we pay the ghost?

231
00:17:20.239 --> 00:17:21.240
Pay the what?

232
00:17:21.340 --> 00:17:22.375
Next.

233
00:17:22.775 --> 00:17:24.914
Right, uh, yeah, a swirled cone

234
00:17:25.011 --> 00:17:26.388
with rainbow sprinkles, please.

235
00:17:26.445 --> 00:17:27.890
Okay. Six bucks.

236
00:17:28.247 --> 00:17:29.282
Yeah.

237
00:17:30.116 --> 00:17:31.186
Keep the change.

238
00:17:36.222 --> 00:17:37.223
Charlie?

239
00:17:37.957 --> 00:17:38.958
Charlie!

240
00:17:40.626 --> 00:17:42.546
- Next!
- Did you see where my son went?

241
00:17:42.962 --> 00:17:44.066
Uh-uh.

242
00:17:44.463 --> 00:17:46.204
- Charlie.
- Who's next?

243
00:17:48.267 --> 00:17:49.268
Charlie!

244
00:17:51.704 --> 00:17:52.876
Where are you?

245
00:17:55.641 --> 00:17:56.711
Charlie!

246
00:18:04.250 --> 00:18:05.251
Charlie!

247
00:18:08.454 --> 00:18:09.455
Charlie.

248
00:18:10.990 --> 00:18:12.060
Hey!

249
00:18:13.125 --> 00:18:14.126
Let him go!

250
00:18:14.794 --> 00:18:15.795
What are you doing?

251
00:18:16.596 --> 00:18:17.631
Charlie!

252
00:18:18.831 --> 00:18:20.003
Charlie, where are you?

253
00:18:22.835 --> 00:18:23.939
Charlie!

254
00:18:28.841 --> 00:18:30.013
This is my son's hat!

255
00:18:30.810 --> 00:18:31.754
The boy that was
wearing this hat,

256
00:18:31.811 --> 00:18:33.449
- did you see him?
- Sir, are you okay?

257
00:18:33.512 --> 00:18:34.633
My son was wearing this hat!

258
00:18:34.647 --> 00:18:36.126
- Sir... Hey, Buddy!
- Charlie!

259
00:18:36.349 --> 00:18:37.869
Officer, Officer,
this is my son's hat.

260
00:18:37.917 --> 00:18:38.987
He's missing!

261
00:18:39.085 --> 00:18:40.086
When did you see him last?

262
00:18:40.152 --> 00:18:41.290
He was right here by
the ice cream truck,

263
00:18:41.354 --> 00:18:42.314
he was right next to me.

264
00:18:42.355 --> 00:18:43.698
Have you tried calling him'?

265
00:18:43.789 --> 00:18:45.769
He's seven years old,
he doesn't have a phone.

266
00:18:45.825 --> 00:18:46.997
Sir, do you live around here?

267
00:18:47.093 --> 00:18:48.197
Maybe he just went home.

268
00:19:04.944 --> 00:19:06.787
- Charlie!
- Mike what's wrong?

269
00:19:07.213 --> 00:19:08.783
- Is he here?
- What's wrong, what's wrong?

270
00:19:08.848 --> 00:19:10.953
Where's Charlie?
Where's Charlie!

271
00:19:11.017 --> 00:19:12.792
I was holding his hand,
I looked everywhere!

272
00:19:12.852 --> 00:19:14.991
What are you telling me?
